  {
   "id": 26,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    -1020,
    0
   ],
   "size": [
    460,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 25,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# 7 - Stable high-resolution subject crop, regeneration and restoration\n\n**Models** (official Comfy-Org files; the loaders carry their download links): ref2va, Qwen3-VL, video + audio VAE.\n\n**Checkpoint variants**: the bf16 checkpoints work in the same loaders (pick them in the list); the Turbo LoRA (4-step ref2v / 8-step fl2v) cuts the steps - set the scheduler steps to match.\n\n**Inputs**: the plate and a mask video of the subject.\n\n**Controls**: Subject Crop (Advanced): one stable box for the clip, upscaled to upscale_megapixels (2 MP here) on the 32 px grid; the crop is encoded into the latent (Inject Video Latent) and re-sampled at denoise 0.45 (raise for more change); Detail Match restores measured sharpness + plate grain; Plate Restore registers (sub-pixel offset), matches colour and pastes back inside the mask only.\n\n**Output**: the plate with a sharper subject, plate sound, MP4.\n\n**Limits**: denoise trades detail against faithfulness; the area outside the mask is the plate.\n\n**Status**: built in ComfyUI's own front end and validated by the server (only missing model / media files reported). NOT run on H3 weights on the build machine - starting values follow core's H3 templates (res_multistep, simple, 20 steps, guider cfg 1). Guide: workflows/tasks/README.md."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "# 7 - Stable high-resolution subject crop, regeneration and restoration\n\n**Models** (official Comfy-Org files; the loaders carry their download links): ref2va, Qwen3-VL, video + audio VAE.\n\n**Checkpoint variants**: the bf16 checkpoints work in the same loaders (pick them in the list); the Turbo LoRA (4-step ref2v / 8-step fl2v) cuts the steps - set the scheduler steps to match.\n\n**Inputs**: the plate and a mask video of the subject.\n\n**Controls**: Subject Crop (Advanced): one stable box for the clip, upscaled to upscale_megapixels (2 MP here) on the 32 px grid; the crop is encoded into the latent (Inject Video Latent) and re-sampled at denoise 0.45 (raise for more change); Detail Match restores measured sharpness + plate grain; Plate Restore registers (sub-pixel offset), matches colour and pastes back inside the mask only.\n\n**Output**: the plate with a sharper subject, plate sound, MP4.\n\n**Limits**: denoise trades detail against faithfulness; the area outside the mask is the plate.\n\n**Status**: built in ComfyUI's own front end and validated by the server (only missing model / media files reported). NOT run on H3 weights on the build machine - starting values follow core's H3 templates (res_multistep, simple, 20 steps, guider cfg 1). Guide: workflows/tasks/README.md."
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
 ],
